{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 210317, "name": "Salam ELIAS", "username": "eliassal", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-03-17T13:30:32.405Z", "cooked": "<p>I am trying to upgrade my fedora35 box to 37, I am following instructions by using<br>\ndnf system-upgrade download --releasever=37</p>\n<p>I get blocked with 3 errors as follows:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Error:<br>\nProblem 1: package rubygem-thin-1.8.0-1.fc34.x86_64 requires libruby.so.3.0()(64bit), but none of the providers can be installed</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ruby-libs-3.0.5-155.fc35.x86_64 does not belong to a distupgrade repository</li>\n<li>problem with installed package rubygem-thin-1.8.0-1.fc34.x86_64<br>\nProblem 2: conflicting requests</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-configs-1.26.0-6.fc37.noarch conflicts with systemd-oomd-defaults provided by systemd-oomd-defaults-251.7-611.fc37.noarch</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-configs-1.26.0-6.fc37.noarch conflicts with systemd-oomd-defaults provided by systemd-oomd-defaults-251.13-6.fc37.noarch</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-1.26.0-6.fc37.x86_64 requires mate-desktop-configs = 1.26.0-6.fc37, but none of the providers can be installed</li>\n<li>problem with installed package mate-desktop-1.26.0-1.fc35.x86_64</li>\n<li>systemd-oomd-defaults-249.13-6.fc35.noarch does not belong to a distupgrade repository</li>\n<li>mate-desktop-1.26.0-1.fc35.x86_64 does not belong to a distupgrade repository<br>\nProblem 3: problem with installed package systemd-oomd-defaults-249.13-6.fc35.noarch</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-configs-1.26.0-6.fc37.noarch conflicts with systemd-oomd-defaults provided by systemd-oomd-defaults-251.7-611.fc37.noarch</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-configs-1.26.0-6.fc37.noarch conflicts with systemd-oomd-defaults provided by systemd-oomd-defaults-251.13-6.fc37.noarch</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-1.26.0-6.fc37.x86_64 requires mate-desktop-configs = 1.26.0-6.fc37, but none of the providers can be installed</li>\n<li>package mate-system-monitor-1.26.0-3.fc37.x86_64 requires mate-desktop, but none of the providers can be installed</li>\n<li>package systemd-oomd-defaults-249.13-6.fc35.noarch requires systemd = 249.13-6.fc35, but none of the providers can be installed</li>\n<li>problem with installed package mate-system-monitor-1.26.0-1.fc35.x86_64</li>\n<li>package mate-desktop-1.26.0-1.fc35.x86_64 requires mate-desktop-libs(x86-64) = 1.26.0-1.fc35, but none of the providers can be installed</li>\n<li>systemd-249.13-6.fc35.x86_64 does not belong to a distupgrade repository</li>\n<li>mate-system-monitor-1.26.0-1.fc35.x86_64 does not belong to a distupgrade repository</li>\n<li>mate-desktop-libs-1.26.0-1.fc35.x86_64 does not belong to a distupgrade repository<br>\n(try to add ‘–allowerasing’ to command line to replace conflicting packages or ‘–skip-broken’ to skip uninstallable packages)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I tried ‘–allowerasing’  and  ‘–skip-broken’, command runs but after a while the terminal just shut down. Can you please tell me what I should do in order to make the upgrade goes through? Than ks in advance</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T14:52:29.673Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 99, "reads": 9, "readers_count": 8, "score": 496.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Salam ELIAS", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10981, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210321, "name": "straycat", "username": "straycat", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/straycat/{size}/6886_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-17T14:00:51.794Z", "cooked": "<p>I’m sure you have but have you made sure that your system is fully up to date.Since F35 is not supported any more I don’t know if it will update.Also you might try and remove rubygem as you can always reinstall it again later.I haven’t used Mate in many years but you might try and upgrade to F36 then upgrade to F37.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-17T14:00:51.794Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 1.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "straycat", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 850, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210341, "name": "Salam ELIAS", "username": "eliassal", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-03-17T15:34:49.832Z", "cooked": "<p>Tim I tried to upgrade to 36, getting the exact same errors</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-17T15:34:49.832Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 1.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Salam ELIAS", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10981, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210402, "name": "straycat", "username": "straycat", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/straycat/{size}/6886_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-18T02:31:04.374Z", "cooked": "<p>Other than trying to remove ruby and trying again I’m sorry I don’t know what else to suggest.I hope someone who knows more about upgrading Mate can read this post and try and help you.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-18T02:31:04.374Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 11.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "straycat", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 850, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210406, "name": "Jeff V", "username": "computersavvy", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/computersavvy/{size}/4741_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-18T02:50:46.013Z", "cooked": "<p>Try the following<br>\n<code>dnf upgrade --refresh</code><br>\n<code>dnf distro-sync --refresh</code></p>\n<p>Fix any errors reported in either of those 2 processes before attempting to do an upgrade to a newer version.  As noted, it may be necessary to uninstall conflicting packages to proceed.<br>\nIt also may be necessary to uninstall packages from 3rd party repos and possibly even disable those repos before proceding.</p>\n<p>Essentially the issue is that if you have something that is not directly upgraded with the new version you may need to remove it before upgrading.</p>\n<p>I note that some of the complaints are about fc34 packages so that would be what I looked at first.  Are they needed or can they be removed?  Anything that can be removed can usually be reinstalled after the upgrades are completed.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-18T02:50:46.013Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 16.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Jeff V", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Q&A Leader", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 3019, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/5", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210430, "name": "Salam ELIAS", "username": "eliassal", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-03-18T14:05:38.794Z", "cooked": "<p>So many thanks JeffV, I did remove the ruby and upgrade went through and I was able to log to the fedora 37. However, I will try to benefit from this thread to ask for another similar issue for a 2nd fedora 35. When I run the</p>\n<p>dnf upgrade --refresh</p>\n<p>I get the following</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Error: Transaction test error:<br>\nfile /usr/share/doc/expat/Changes from install of expat-2.5.0-1.fc35.i686 conflicts with file from package expat-2.4.9-1.fc35.x86_64<br>\nfile /usr/share/man/man1/xmlwf.1.gz from install of expat-2.5.0-1.fc35.i686 conflicts with file from package expat-2.4.9-1.fc35.x86_64<br>\nfile /usr/share/doc/libxcrypt/NEWS from install of libxcrypt-4.4.33-3.fc35.i686 conflicts with file from package libxcrypt-4.4.28-1.fc35.x86_64</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>When I try to remove expat<br>\nsudo dnf remove expat --skip-broken<br>\nor<br>\nsudo dnf remove expat expat-2.4.9-1.fc35.x86_64 --skip-broken<br>\nI get an alert</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Error:<br>\nProblem: The operation would result in removing the following protected packages: systemd</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Soreally stuck and refresh never goes through even when I use --skip-broken or --exclude=expat-2.4.9-1.fc35.x86_64</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-18T14:05:38.794Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 21.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Salam ELIAS", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10981, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210431, "name": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "username": "vgaetera", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vgaetera/{size}/2552_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-18T14:26:19.941Z", "cooked": "<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">sudo dnf remove expat.i686 libxcrypt.i686\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-20T21:27:00.532Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 6.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 10981, "username": "eliassal", "name": "Salam ELIAS", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 549, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/7", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210557, "name": "Salam ELIAS", "username": "eliassal", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-03-19T09:34:19.586Z", "cooked": "<p>So many thanks Vladislav, the 1st statement did the job and<br>\n<code>sudo dnf upgrade --refresh</code><br>\ngoes well and rebooted after it was successful. However, when I run</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>sudo dnf system-upgrade download --releasever=37</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It downloads files then it starts transaction check and all of a suydden terminal shuts down by itself, this happened 3 times</p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-19T09:34:19.586Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 6.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Salam ELIAS", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10981, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/8", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210567, "name": "Matthew Miller", "username": "mattdm", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/mattdm/{size}/2450_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-19T12:03:50.260Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"eliassal\" data-post=\"8\" data-topic=\"79588\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Salam ELIAS:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It downloads files then it starts transaction check and all of a suydden terminal shuts down by itself, this happened 3 times</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Are you running out of memory?</p>", "post_number": 9, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-19T12:03:50.260Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 8, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 8, "readers_count": 7, "score": 11.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79588, "topic_slug": "mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37", "display_username": "Matthew Miller", "primary_group_name": "discussion-bots", "flair_name": "discussion-bots", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 52, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Flock 2013 Speaker", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 10981, "username": "eliassal", "name": "Salam ELIAS", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/38bc3b/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": true, "admin": true, "staff": true, "group_moderator": true, "user_id": 5, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/mate-desktop-configs-rubygem-thin-1-8-0-1-fc34-x86-64-not-allowing-upgrade-from-35-to-37/79588/9", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 210576, "name": "Matthew Miller", "username": "mattdm", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/mattdm/{size}/2450_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-19T13:21:22.236Z", "cooked": "<p>If you are running out of memory — and the out-of-memory killer stopping the process in an attempt to keep this from making the system responsive would explain what you’re seeing — see this:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"76389\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/adamwill/48/377_2.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <div class=\"quote-title__text-content\">\n      <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/dnf-operations-use-large-amount-of-ram-and-may-fail-in-low-memory-environments/76389\">DNF operations use large amount of RAM and may fail in low-memory environments</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ask/common-issues/common-issues-archived/87\"><span data-category-id=\"87\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #808281; --category-badge-text-color: #000000; --parent-category-badge-color: #e59728;\" data-parent-category-id=\"82\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square --has-parent\" title=\"This is a collection of Common Issues from past Fedora Linux releases. This format started with Fedora Linux 36. For common bugs pages from earlier than that, see this list of links to pre-F35 Common Bugs pages.\"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">Archived Common Issues</span></span></a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    <a name=\"p-180338-problem-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-180338-problem-1\"></a>Problem\n\nThe current design of the DNF package manager can cause it to use quite large amounts of memory (into the hundreds of megabytes) for most operations. This can mean that DNF operations fail (due to being killed by the kernel’s out-of-memory handler) in low-memory environments, especially systems or containers with 1GB or less of memory and no swap space. \n<a name=\"p-180338-cause-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-180338-cause-2\"></a>Cause\n\n\nThis is due to parsing large amounts of repository metadata, and the exact amount of memory used varies over time and between …\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n", "post_number": 10, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 11, "updated_at": "2023-03-19T13:21:22.236Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 9, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 5, "reads": 9, "readers_cou